Revision history for Mojolicious-Plugin-Heimdall

0.002
          - Resolve active accounts in the route guard and memoize per request.
          - Restrict post-login redirects to local paths and clear CSRF state at login/logout.
          - Reject default or weakly configured production session signing secrets.
          - Add verify_access_token with algorithm, issuer, audience, expiry, and subject checks.
          - Ship a CSRF-protected sign-in example with a separate admin authorization check.
          - Build and install the source distribution in CI. Require Mojolicious 9.48+ and CryptX 0.091+.

0.001     2026-11-06
          - Initial release
          - Password hashing via Crypt::Passphrase (Argon2 default, Bcrypt verify)
          - Secure random tokens via Crypt::URandom::Token
          - RSA (OAEP) and AES-GCM via CryptX
          - JWS and JWE via Crypt::JWT
          - Session authentication on top of Mojolicious::Sessions
          - Unified facade: $c->heimdall->password / random / crypto / jwt / auth
          - docs/ with numbered copy-pasteable examples
